# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# firmware/ is ALL build output, not source.
#
# It holds the sdcard image (2.6 GB), the ROM partition (2.0 GB), kernels,
# DTBs, u-boot, the launcher binary, built cores, and several staging snapshots
# (fix/ psx/ rot/ push/) taken while iterating against the board. Every one is
# reproducible:
#     scripts/rebuild_image.sh   -> sdcard.img, zImage, dtbs, u-boot
#     scripts/stage-push.sh      -> the staging copies
#
# Git stores a full copy of every changed binary, so tracking these would add
# gigabytes per rebuild. An earlier version of this file only excluded *.img
# and *.vfat, which still let 31.6 MB of stale binaries into the first commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
firmware/

# ROM archives: large, regenerable, and not ours to distribute.
backup/*.tar.gz

# Scratch
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej

# NOTE: buildroot-external/package/retroarch/retroarch/retro-assets IS tracked
# deliberately -- retroarch.mk:45 copies it into the target, so it is a build
# input, not an output.
